task: intent-window-by-dim (the n-gram window against the per-class law at each hash width; the wider-hash half measured)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/intent-window-by-dim

why: intent-typo-robustness left one question unmeasured: a narrower
  window keeps its typo robustness and loses `Other` at the shipped
  width 1024 -- does it keep `Other` at 4096? `TestModels`' per-class
  law (every class F1 >= 0.50, majority baseline < 0.40) runs on the
  shipped artifact only. Measure per-class F1 (Eval.Confusion) for
  (3,5), (2,4), (2,3) at 1024 and 4096 on the TestModels held-out half,
  clean and under the typo, in one default-gate suite. If (2,4)@4096
  keeps every class, the default window can move together with Fit's
  dim; if not, the answer is rows (intent-other-more-rows). No default
  moves in this lane; the number decides the next one.
